.nh
.TH "GH-ISSUE-ARTIFACT-CREATE" "1" "Oct 2026" "GitHub CLI 2.103.3" "GitHub CLI manual"

.SH NAME
gh-issue-artifact-create - Create issue artifacts (preview)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgh issue artifact create {<issue-number> | <issue-url>} [<file>[#<name>] | <url>]... [flags]\fR


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create one artifact for each file or URL. A text file becomes a document
named after the file; add \fB#<name>\fR to choose a different name. A \fB\&.html\fR or
\fB\&.htm\fR file becomes an HTML document. A URL, or a \fB\&.url\fR Internet Shortcut
file, becomes a link; a URL is named after its host.

.PP
Artifact names can't contain some characters, such as parentheses. When a
file's name has them, they're removed: \fBplan (1).md\fR is named \fBplan 1.md\fR\&.

.PP
Use \fB--body\fR to create a single document from text, or \fB--body-file\fR to create
one artifact from a file (\fB-\fR reads standard input). \fB--name\fR sets its name.

.PP
Documents are saved as \fBgeneric\fR, and HTML documents as \fBembedded_html\fR\&. Use
\fB--type\fR to set the type of every document instead, whatever the file
extension. A plan currently behaves the same as a generic document.


.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--attach\fR \fB<file>\fR
Attach an image or video file, in '#\&' format

.TP
\fB-b\fR, \fB--body\fR \fB<string>\fR
Content for a single document

.TP
\fB-F\fR, \fB--body-file\fR \fB<file>\fR
Read content for a single artifact from file (use "-" to read from standard input)

.TP
\fB--name\fR \fB<string>\fR
Name for a single artifact

.TP
\fB--type\fR \fB<string>\fR
Type for documents: {generic|plan|embedded_html}


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
.TP
\fB-R\fR, \fB--repo\fR \fB<[HOST/]OWNER/REPO>\fR
Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format


.SH ALIASES
gh issue artifact new


.SH EXIT CODES
0: Successful execution

.PP
1: Error

.PP
2: Command canceled

.PP
4: Authentication required

.PP
NOTE: Specific commands may have additional exit codes. Refer to the command's help for more information.


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
# Create a document from a file
$ gh issue artifact create 142 signin-plan.md

# Create documents from two files, naming the first
$ gh issue artifact create 142 'docs/signin-plan.md#Sign-in plan' oauth-research.md

# Create an HTML document from a file
$ gh issue artifact create 142 menu-prototype.html

# Create a link with a name
$ gh issue artifact create 142 https://github.com/monalisa/monas-cafe/wiki/OAuth-runbook --name 'Staging OAuth runbook'

# Create a document from standard input
$ cat order-sync.log | gh issue artifact create 142 --body-file - --name 'Order sync log'

# Upload an image that the document references
$ gh issue artifact create 142 signin-plan.md --attach ./signin-flow.png

.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgh-issue-artifact(1)\fR
